--- A function that answers a view's call directly (`return cell[s]`, or `cell[s]`
--- as its last line) does not build compiled; the interpreter prints <td>a &lt; b</td>.
---   compiled: error[E0308]: mismatched types
---               --> src/main.rs:45:12
---             error: the compiled program does not build — the Rust compiler refused
---             what Crow accepted, a bug in Crow, not in this program
--- The function is typed as answering text (markup), and the emitter writes
--- `return cell(s);` where cell answers a CrowVNode: the node is not rendered
--- (`.to_html()`), as it is when the call is first given to a local
--- (`m = cell[s]` / `return m` builds and prints the same as interpreted).
--- Expected: <td>a &lt; b</td> in both modes.
use web, ui

view cell[s]
    return td[s]

fn markup_of[s]
    return cell[s]

log[markup_of['a < b']]
